From: linux-omarchy-aarch64
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: syscon: do not attach a clock provider's parent clock

syscon treats the first clocks entry as the register-access clock and
keeps it prepared. On the X1E TCSR clock provider that entry is the
parent clock, bi_tcxo. Holding it prepared pins an RPMh XO vote, so the
crystal stays on through s2idle.

Skip clocks on a node that has #clock-cells. Other syscon users are
unchanged.

Source: https://github.com/justririll/x1e-sleep/blob/4e84b60eb0/kernel/sleep/syscon-skip-clock-of-clock-providers.patch

---
diff --git a/drivers/mfd/syscon.c b/drivers/mfd/syscon.c
--- a/drivers/mfd/syscon.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/syscon.c
@@ -123,7 +123,16 @@
 	}
 
 	if (check_res) {
-		clk = of_clk_get(np, 0);
+		/*
+		 * The "clocks" of a clock provider (the X1E TCSR block) are its
+		 * parent clocks, not a register clock. Attaching one keeps it
+		 * prepared forever and pins an RPMh XO vote, so the crystal stays
+		 * on through suspend.
+		 */
+		if (of_property_present(np, "#clock-cells"))
+			clk = ERR_PTR(-ENOENT);
+		else
+			clk = of_clk_get(np, 0);
 		if (IS_ERR(clk)) {
 			ret = PTR_ERR(clk);
 			/* clock is optional */
